Here's a function in C# that inserts a character into a string at a given index:

```csharp
using System;

public class StringManipulator
{
    public static string InsertCharacter(string input, int index, char character)
    {
        if (input == null)
            return string.Empty;

        if (index < 0)
            return input;

        if (index > input.Length)
            return input + character.ToString();

        char[] charArray = input.ToCharArray();

        charArray.Insert(index, character);

        return new string(charArray);
    }
}
```

### Usage Example:

```csharp
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        string original = "Hello";
        char newChar = 'x';
        int position = 3;

        string result = StringManipulator.InsertCharacter(original, position, newChar);
        Console.WriteLine(result); // Output: Hellox
    }
}
```

